{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1519079-chronicle-idea\u2026-needs-fleshing-out","id":1519079,"title":"Chronicle Idea\u2026 Needs Fleshing Out","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-29T00:43:44-07:00","id":1519079,"title":"Chronicle Idea\u2026 Needs Fleshing Out","content":"<i>Saw </i>film franchise but in Arcadia. The players were all kept by a True Fae version of John Kramer who forced them to play his twisted deadly games forever and ever and ever. I want there to be an Amanda Young type character at some point (or the guy from <i>Spiral</i> who had it out for cops) who is, unbeknownst to the players, still allied with their Keeper.<br /> <br /> This idea has been living in my head rent free for too long. It\u2019s not fleshed out enough to make a chronicle imo. Any help/advice/thoughts would be greatly appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","name":"trynmybest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27935_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T04:13:08-07:00","id":1519098,"title":"","content":"I don't know Saw well enough, but do they need a keeper? What if the players all start out as mortals, a group of friends pledged to always help each other, but when one goes missing the rest go and search...<br /> <br /> Ok, this is the idea that they start out as Fae-touched wandering the hedge, eventually they may end up in Arcadia, possibly becoming hedge ghosts, goblin Queens, Changelings etc along the way (depending on how badly/well things go).<br /> <br /> But yeah, that is my own idea for a one-shot, which i think makes a nice prelude to your chronicle. Gives you a reason for the player characters to trust each other, and in a Saw movie where they will later he expected to break that trust it seems pretty good to have a nice background...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T10:20:10-07:00","id":1519264,"title":"","content":"So my whole reasoning behind the players having a Keeper really lies in the basis of Kramer\u2019s MO &amp; how his traps/games work. I\u2019m not sure how much of the franchise you\u2019re familiar with but everything Kramer does as Jigsaw boils down to two things: choice &amp; redemption. The players in his games are forced to acknowledge their past choices got them into the situation they find themselves in. They all made choices which were criminal in some form \u2014 even those who chose to do nothing \u2014 many ending in death. Which is why they\u2019re always asked to make another choice at the beginning of each game. Live or die. Those who prove they\u2019re worthy of redemption and salvation do so through playing the game.<br /> <br /> And I think those themes work best if the players have, or at least had, a Keeper.<br /> <br /> Your idea of the players starting as Fae-touched &amp; ending up in Arcadia is a good idea though. May keep that in my back pocket in case I can\u2019t come up with anything else.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","name":"trynmybest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27935_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T11:30:43-07:00","id":1519272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trynmybest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1519079-chronicle-idea\u2026-needs-fleshing-out?p=1519264#post1519264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my whole reasoning behind the players having a Keeper really lies in the basis of Kramer\u2019s MO &amp; how his traps/games work. I\u2019m not sure how much of the franchise you\u2019re familiar with but everything Kramer does as Jigsaw boils down to two things: choice &amp; redemption. The players in his games are forced to acknowledge their past choices got them into the situation they find themselves in. They all made choices which were criminal in some form \u2014 even those who chose to do nothing \u2014 many ending in death. Which is why they\u2019re always asked to make another choice at the beginning of each game. Live or die. Those who prove they\u2019re worthy of redemption and salvation do so through playing the game.<br /> <br /> And I think those themes work best if the players have, or at least had, a Keeper.<br /> <br /> Your idea of the players starting as Fae-touched &amp; ending up in Arcadia is a good idea though. May keep that in my back pocket in case I can\u2019t come up with anything else.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a different view of the Saw movies than the small amount of the wikipedia article i read before posting.<br /> <br /> Having a True Fae who takes only those he thinks are 'bad'* might be interesting, and even challenging them to perform what fae thinks of as 'redemptipn' despite not truly understanding what that means, could be a very interesting story.<br /> <br /> I think I am confusing Saw with Cube though... Where you find yourself in this weird labyrinthine death trap/puzzle box (which may just be a challenge to keep the True Fae interested). Could be a session 1 prelude - where the main game starts with everyone escaping but the first session is set during the character's durance(s).<br /> <br /> * Where I presume 'bad' to a True Fae means not living up to some precieved oath/agreement that humans are supposed to follow...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T11:56:14-07:00","id":1519275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is a different view of the Saw movies than the small amount of the wikipedia article i read before posting. </div> </div> </div>Well I don\u2019t know how the wiki sums it up but as an avid fan of the franchise I can say that it\u2019s a lot more nuanced than most people give it credit for. People say it\u2019s just violence &amp; gore but that really only started later on in the franchise. <i>Spiral</i> got the franchise back to its roots &amp; focused on those original running themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Where I presume 'bad' to a True Fae means not living up to some precieved oath/agreement that humans are supposed to follow... </div> </div> </div>Yeah that\u2019s pretty much exactly what I was thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","name":"trynmybest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27935_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}